{
  "quest.0ACAF0EA709D9E0B.title": "Where Do Noble Gases Come From?",
  "quest.01600AF0D4EC1438.title": "Battery Box",
  "quest.0637A970EF2AE227.title": "Higher-Tier Circuits",
  "quest.2A7018846454F62F.quest_desc": [
    "The Silicon Dioxide in the recipes can be replaced with any Quartz Dust or Quartzite Dust.",
    "",
    "GT6's circuits aren't designed as nested tiers, nor are they locked down as hard as in gt5. Circuits come in 6 tiers and are backward compatible. Crystal Processors are the exception.",
    "",
    "The parts making up a Circuit Board are the Circuit Plate, Circuit Part, Etched Circuit and Solder. The first three also come in 6 tiers and follow the barrel principle. The fourth applies an extra tier penalty to the finished board (Lead -2, Tin -1, Solder 0).",
  ],
  "quest.0C9CFAECE40EEF16.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond Crystal Processors are used the least, Ruby Crystal Processors the most.",
    "",
    "Congratulations on reaching the late Electric Age! Large machines are unlocked! All late-game electric machines are unlocked!",
  ],
  "quest.36D33A53FE71B9E0.quest_desc": [
    "It can process most ore dusts.",
  ],
  "quest.1707E46AA4050289.quest_desc": [
    "Silicon is obtained by reducing Silicon Dioxide in a Crucible.",
    "",
    "In the Crucible, Silicon Dioxide can be replaced with Quartzite and any Quartz. Or centrifuge Molten Glass to obtain Silicon Dioxide.",
  ],
  "quest.2A7018846454F62F.quest_subtitle": "The beginning of electronic circuits",
  "quest.7C1414368D9F6817.title": "Crystallisation Crucible",
  "quest.0637A970EF2AE227.quest_desc": [
    "Congratulations - you're now qualified to make higher-tier circuits.",
    "",
    "If you don't have platinum processing, make Advanced Circuits.",
    "",
    "If you have plenty of Platinum from platinum processing, make Ultimate Circuits.",
  ],
  "quest.64A5B458586AEC5E.quest_desc": [
    "Cryo-distilling Air gives Nitrogen, Oxygen, Carbon Dioxide, Sulfur Dioxide and noble gases.",
    "",
    "Its most important use is obtaining noble gases.",
    "",
    "Processing Air and Nether Air gives trace amounts of Helium, Neon and Argon.",
    "",
    "Processing Ender Air gives trace amounts of Krypton, Xenon and Radon.",
    "",
    "Since you'll need lots of Helium and Neon later, start idling this early.",
  ],
  "quest.1B169D16D60874FA.quest_desc": [
    "The Hand Drill can bind placed mining Dynamite or Gunpowder Sticks to a Remote Activator.",
    "",
    "Right-click to ignite all bound explosives.",
  ],
  "quest.607AF01115BBF1D6.quest_desc": [
    "Electricity has voltage and current settings, and its mechanics are basically the same as in GT5.",
    "",
    "Voltage tiers: 1-16 EU/t is Ultra Low Voltage (ULV), 16-64 is Low Voltage (LV), 64-256 is Medium Voltage (MV), 256-1024 is High Voltage (HV), 1024-4096 is Extreme Voltage (EV), 4096-16384 is Insane Voltage (IV), 16384-65536 is Ludicrous Voltage (LuV), 65536-262144 is Zero Point Voltage (ZPM), 262144-1048576 is Ultimate Voltage (UV), and above 1048576 is Super Ultimate Voltage (PUV).",
    "",
    "Power is only accepted when the voltage matches the machine's tier.",
    "",
    "It can be carried by Wires, with some loss; mind the Wires' voltage and current limits.",
    "",
    "Touching an uninsulated Wire while it is live will hurt you.",
    "",
    "It can be stored in Batteries placed inside a Battery Box.",
    "",
    "An extremely important energy source: it's the first energy type that can be stored on a large scale, and it can be converted into almost every other kind of energy!",
  ],
  "quest.00B2D0654ED7F7C8.quest_desc": [
    "Normally used to make Etched Circuits and Crystal Circuits, and it can also etch Bricks for decoration. Advanced Etched Circuits absolutely require this machine.",
  ],
  "quest.414D899FB86A7AA9.quest_desc": [
    "Three crystals can be used for electronic components: Monocrystalline Silicon, Monocrystalline Germanium and Monocrystalline Redstone Alloy (Red Silicon).",
    "",
    "They must be cut into Crystalline Plates and then into Tiny Crystalline Plates before electronic components can be made.",
    "",
    "The three crystals differ slightly:",
    "Basic/Good electronic components can be made from all three;",
    "Advanced electronic components can't be made from Red Silicon;",
    "Elite electronic components can only be made from Red Silicon;",
    "Master electronic components can't be made from Red Silicon;",
    "Ultimate electronic components can only be made from Red Silicon.",
    "",
    "Pretty amazing, right?",
    "",
    "Silicon is obtained by reducing Silicon Dioxide in a Crucible.",
    "",
    "In the Crucible, Silicon Dioxide can be replaced with Quartzite and any Quartz. Or centrifuge Molten Glass to obtain Silicon Dioxide.",
  ],
  "quest.0C9CFAECE40EEF16.title": "Crystal Processor",
  "quest.67FB9F1692E2266B.quest_desc": [
    "You may have already found some Lighters in loot chests; if not, make one.",
    "",
    "The Plastic Lighter (BIC) is the only craftable Lighter; it needs Plastic and also needs filling with a Canning Machine.",
    "",
    "The Plastic Lighter breaks once used up, and the broken one can be recycled in a Crucible or a Shredder.",
  ],
  "quest.2597D57B88836E35.quest_desc": [
    "Normally used to make Etched Circuits and Crystal Circuits, and it can also etch Bricks for decoration. Advanced Etched Circuits absolutely require this machine.",
  ],
  "quest.663629D0C593DDD6.quest_desc": [
    "4x and larger Cables must be insulated in the Laminator.",
  ],
  "quest.1BF89AA525338398.quest_desc": [
    "Basic Circuits save some material, but the difference from the lower-tier circuit is actually tiny. Since GT6's circuits are backward compatible, it's recommended to make the lower-tier circuit directly.",
  ],
  "quest.79526AE637161944.quest_desc": [
    "The Automatic Machine Switch turns machines on/off as needed and stops them from going into standby (idle electric machines drain power, and with a Battery Box attached they'll drain it dry). It also automatically starts/stops the Electric Engines/Diesel Engines/Electromagnets that power machines. However, it can only switch off blocks directly adjacent to itself.",
    "",
    "If the power-supplying machine isn't adjacent to the machine, use a combination of an Activity Detector (Possible) and a Redstone Machine Switch.",
    "",
    "The Activity Detector (Possible) outputs a redstone signal while the machine is running a recipe or its recipe inputs are satisfied.",
    "",
    "The Redstone Machine Switch can also be used with other sensors, e.g. with an Energy Sensor to check a Battery Box's charge and start/stop the generator automatically.",
    "",
    "No more worrying about fuel engines burning for nothing - spend your first circuits on these and upgrade your ore processing and workshop.",
  ],
  "quest.616B11528D22D5CE.quest_subtitle": "Just do any one of the lines",
  "quest.2597D57B88836E35.quest_subtitle": "Just do any one of the lines",
  "quest.663629D0C593DDD6.title": "Laminator",
  "quest.0ACAF0EA709D9E0B.quest_desc": [
    "The noble gases are Helium, Neon, Argon, Krypton, Xenon and Radon.",
    "",
    "The easiest way to get noble gas for the Crystallisation Crucible is centrifuging Fluorite Dust for Helium.",
    "",
    "You'll need the other noble gases later.",
    "",
    "Neon, Krypton, Xenon and Radon can only be obtained from the Cryo Distillation Tower.",
  ],
  "quest.5A28BD71AADF82CE.quest_desc": [
    "A better electrical material than Copper.",
    "",
    "In reality Annealed Copper needs electrolytic refining, but here you only need to heat Copper to 2800 K.",
    "",
    "If you want it before progressing the LV main line, use a Meteoric Steel or Iridium Crucible.",
    "",
    "&cNote: this temperature is close to the Meteoric Steel Crucible's temperature limit and to Copper's boiling point!&r",
  ],
  "quest.58909744EAF18360.quest_desc": [
    "Used to fill various Lighters, Lasers, Batteries and Fuel Rods/Breeder Rods.",
  ],
  "quest.414D899FB86A7AA9.title": "Monocrystalline Silicon",
  "quest.607AF01115BBF1D6.title": "About Electricity",
  "quest.52C2CB0D21AC48F8.quest_desc": [
    "Consumes electricity and outputs both CU (Cold Energy) and HU.",
    "",
    "CU can be supplied to the Cryo Distillation Tower and the Cryo Mixer, and when supplied to Crucibles and Molds it helps cool them down.",
  ],
  "quest.7CE8645C204AB306.quest_subtitle": "The beginning of the Electric Age",
  "quest.7CE8645C204AB306.quest_desc": [
    "The Electric Age is where GT6 really shines.",
    "",
    "If your Crucible line has produced an Iridium Crucible (Niobium Titanium Carbide is unlocked later) and you have plenty of Iridium at home, you can get one now and feed an HV Electric Dynamo.",
    "",
    "&cNote: a Dynamo's output current is fixed at 1 A, and the input rotation speed affects the voltage. A fully upgraded LV Electric Dynamo (44 EU/t) will burn Tin Cables (32 EU/t)!&r",
  ],
  "quest.52C2CB0D21AC48F8.title": "Thermoelectric Cooler",
  "quest.01600AF0D4EC1438.quest_desc": [
    "A Battery Box can hold Batteries to store EU and can also charge electric tools.",
    "",
    "The Battery Box's maximum output current equals the number of Batteries.",
    "",
    "Batteries can't be a higher tier than the Battery Box.",
    "",
    "Battery Boxes at LUV and above are pointless.",
    "",
    "The Battery Box's output voltage is fixed, as follows:",
    "ULV: 8",
    "LV: 32",
    "MV: 128",
    "HV: 512",
    "EV: 2048",
    "IV: 8192",
    "LUV: 32768",
    "ZPM: 131072",
    "UV: 524288",
    "PUV1: 2087152",
    "",
    "Because of this property, Battery Boxes can be used to regulate voltage and limit current.",
  ],
  "quest.278585C7C54F4C26.quest_desc": [
    "Electrolyzing ore dusts, electrolyzing the various kinds of Water and producing Aluminium are all its job.",
    "",
    "Later you can build the large multiblock version, which has lossless overclocking and parallel processing.",
    "",
    "Unlike gt5, many single-block electric machines don't need a Circuit Board - you're still far from the electric machines that do.",
    "",
    "You can build both LV and HV Electrolyzers already, but supplying HV power is much more of a hassle.",
  ],
  "quest.620F58A0F60FD8A9.quest_desc": [
    "If you want to use an HV Electric Dynamo before progressing the LV main line, power it with an Iridium Diesel Engine.",
  ],
  "quest.1871FB785B68A306.quest_subtitle": "Just do any one of the lines",
  "quest.00B2D0654ED7F7C8.quest_subtitle": "Just do any one of the lines",
  "quest.7C1414368D9F6817.quest_desc": [
    "A machine used to crystallise Silicon and other crystals.",
    "",
    "It can also crystallise Red Silicon, Germanium Crystals, Ruby Crystals and the various Sapphire Crystals.",
    "",
    "The recipes require noble gases.",
  ],
  "quest.337DC97B1142DFB7.quest_desc": [
    "The lowest-tier Circuit Board, and the only Circuit Board that doesn't need the Laser Engraver.",
  ],
}